@page "/events/tutorials/10-manual-registration"

<TutorialDetail Tutorials="TutorialSet.Events" Slug="10-manual-registration">
<p><strong>Goal:</strong> subscribe without <code>[Subscribe]</code> and <code>[UseState]</code>, for the cases attributes can't express: selectors that depend on parameters, custom comparers, conditional or dynamic subscriptions.</p>

<p><em>See it running:</em> <code>TickerTile</code> on the <strong>Live dashboard</strong> sample page (<a href="/events/example/live-dashboard"><code>/events/example/live-dashboard</code></a>).</p>

<h2 id="what-the-attributes-generate">What the attributes generate</h2>

<p>The source generator turns attributes into an override of <code>RegisterSubscriptions</code>. You can write that override yourself, using the same <code>SubscriptionBuilder</code>:</p>

<div class="table-container"><table class="table is-striped">
<thead>
<tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Manual equivalent</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>[UseState] partial T X { get; }</code></td><td><code>_x = builder.State&lt;T&gt;();</code> then read <code>_x.Value</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>[UseState(Select = nameof(S))] partial V X { get; }</code></td><td><code>_x = builder.State&lt;T, V&gt;(S);</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>[Subscribe] void On(E e)</code></td><td><code>builder.On&lt;E&gt;(On);</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Scope = ScopeKind.Root</code> / <code>ScopeName = "n"</code></td><td><code>at: ScopeTarget.Root</code> / <code>ScopeTarget.Named("n")</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Render = false</code></td><td><code>render: false</code></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>

<p><code>RegisterSubscriptions</code> runs <strong>after parameters are set</strong> and <strong>before <code>OnInitialized</code></strong>, which is what makes parameter-dependent selectors possible.</p>

<h2 id="1-a-selector-that-depends-on-a-parameter">1. A selector that depends on a parameter</h2>

<p>Attribute selectors must be <code>static</code>, so they can't see <code>[Parameter]</code> values. A lambda can:</p>

<pre><code>// MyApp.Client/Features/Stocks/PriceState.cs
using System.Collections.Immutable;

namespace MyApp.Client.Features.Stocks;

public sealed record PriceState(ImmutableDictionary&lt;string, decimal&gt; Prices) : IState&lt;PriceState&gt;
{
    public static PriceState Initial =&gt; new(ImmutableDictionary&lt;string, decimal&gt;.Empty);
}

public sealed record PriceChanged(string Symbol, decimal Change) : IEvent;</code></pre>

<pre><code>@@* MyApp.Client/Features/Stocks/Components/PriceTile.razor *@@
@@inherits RfEventComponent

&lt;div class="card text-center"&gt;
    &lt;div class="card-body"&gt;
        &lt;div class="fw-semibold"&gt;@@Symbol&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div class="fs-4"&gt;@@_price.Value.ToString("N2")&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;small&gt;@@(_lastChange &gt;= 0 ? "▲" : "▼")&lt;/small&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>

<pre><code>// MyApp.Client/Features/Stocks/Components/PriceTile.razor.cs
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components;

namespace MyApp.Client.Features.Stocks.Components;

public partial class PriceTile
{
    private SelectorHandle&lt;PriceState, decimal&gt; _price = default!;
    private decimal _lastChange;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string Symbol { get; set; } = "";

    protected override void RegisterSubscriptions(SubscriptionBuilder builder)
    {
        base.RegisterSubscriptions(builder);

        // Symbol is already set here. Re-render only when THIS symbol's price changes.
        _price = builder.State&lt;PriceState, decimal&gt;(p =&gt; p.Prices.GetValueOrDefault(Symbol));

        // Track the direction without a render of its own; the price selector triggers the render.
        builder.On&lt;PriceChanged&gt;(e =&gt;
        {
            if (e.Symbol == Symbol)
            {
                _lastChange = e.Change;
            }
        }, render: false);
    }
}</code></pre>

<blockquote>
<p>Parameters are read <strong>once</strong>, when registering. If <code>Symbol</code> can change for the same component instance, put <code>@@key="symbol"</code> on the component where it's used so Blazor re-creates it instead.</p>
</blockquote>

<h2 id="2-a-custom-comparer">2. A custom comparer</h2>

<p>Selectors compare with default equality. Pass a comparer to change that, for example to ignore case:</p>

<pre><code>// MyApp.Client/Features/Stocks/Components/WatchlistLabel.razor.cs
namespace MyApp.Client.Features.Stocks.Components;

public partial class WatchlistLabel
{
    private SelectorHandle&lt;WatchlistState, string&gt; _name = default!;

    protected override void RegisterSubscriptions(SubscriptionBuilder builder)
    {
        base.RegisterSubscriptions(builder);
        _name = builder.State&lt;WatchlistState, string&gt;(w =&gt; w.Name, comparer: StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
    }
}</code></pre>

<pre><code>@@* MyApp.Client/Features/Stocks/Components/WatchlistLabel.razor *@@
@@inherits RfEventComponent

&lt;h3&gt;@@_name.Value&lt;/h3&gt;</code></pre>

<pre><code>// MyApp.Client/Features/Stocks/WatchlistState.cs
namespace MyApp.Client.Features.Stocks;

public sealed record WatchlistState(string Name) : IState&lt;WatchlistState&gt;
{
    public static WatchlistState Initial =&gt; new("My watchlist");
}</code></pre>

<h2 id="3-mix-attributes-and-manual-code">3. Mix attributes and manual code</h2>

<p>A component with attributes already has a generated <code>RegisterSubscriptions</code>, so <strong>don't override it</strong> (that's error <code>RFEVT009</code>). Implement the generated hook instead, which runs after the generated registrations:</p>

<pre><code>// MyApp.Client/Features/Stocks/Components/PriceAlerts.razor.cs
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components;

namespace MyApp.Client.Features.Stocks.Components;

public partial class PriceAlerts
{
    private readonly List&lt;string&gt; _alerts = [];

    [Parameter]
    public bool IncludeSmallMoves { get; set; }

    [UseState(Select = nameof(SelectCount))]
    private partial int Tracked { get; }

    private static int SelectCount(PriceState prices) =&gt; prices.Prices.Count;

    // Generated by the source generator; runs after the attribute-based registrations.
    partial void OnRegisterSubscriptions(SubscriptionBuilder builder)
    {
        // Conditional subscription: decided once, from a parameter.
        if (IncludeSmallMoves)
        {
            builder.On&lt;PriceChanged&gt;(e =&gt; _alerts.Insert(0, $"{e.Symbol} {e.Change:+0.00;-0.00}"));
        }
        else
        {
            builder.On&lt;PriceChanged&gt;(e =&gt;
            {
                if (Math.Abs(e.Change) &gt;= 1)
                {
                    _alerts.Insert(0, $"{e.Symbol} moved {e.Change:+0.00;-0.00}");
                }
            });
        }
    }
}</code></pre>

<pre><code>@@* MyApp.Client/Features/Stocks/Components/PriceAlerts.razor *@@
@@inherits RfEventComponent

&lt;p&gt;Tracking @@Tracked symbols&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;@@foreach (var alert in _alerts.Take(5)) { &lt;li&gt;@@alert&lt;/li&gt; }&lt;/ul&gt;</code></pre>

<h2 id="4-subscribe-later-or-to-something-decided-at-runtime">4. Subscribe later, or to something decided at runtime</h2>

<p><code>SubscriptionBuilder</code> only works during registration. To subscribe later (after a button click, say), use the scope directly, <strong>marshal to the renderer yourself</strong>, and dispose in <code>DisposeAsyncCore</code>:</p>

<pre><code>// MyApp.Client/Features/Stocks/Components/LiveFeedToggle.razor.cs
namespace MyApp.Client.Features.Stocks.Components;

public partial class LiveFeedToggle
{
    private IDisposable? _subscription;
    private int _received;

    private void Toggle()
    {
        if (_subscription is not null)
        {
            _subscription.Dispose();
            _subscription = null;
            return;
        }

        // Scope.Subscribe is the raw API: no InvokeAsync, no automatic render, no automatic disposal.
        _subscription = Scope.Subscribe&lt;PriceChanged&gt;(async (e, cancellationToken) =&gt;
            await InvokeAsync(() =&gt;
            {
                _received++;
                StateHasChanged();
            }));
    }

    protected override ValueTask DisposeAsyncCore()
    {
        _subscription?.Dispose();
        return ValueTask.CompletedTask;
    }
}</code></pre>

<pre><code>@@* MyApp.Client/Features/Stocks/Components/LiveFeedToggle.razor *@@
@@inherits RfEventComponent

&lt;button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" @@onclick="Toggle"&gt;@@(_subscription is null ? "Listen" : "Stop") (@@_received)&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>

<p>Prefer step 3 (decide at registration) when you can. Late subscriptions are the escape hatch.</p>

<h2 id="how-it-works">How it works</h2>

<ul>
<li><code>SubscriptionBuilder.On</code> and <code>.State</code> wrap your delegate so it runs through <code>InvokeAsync</code>, re-renders (unless <code>render: false</code>), routes exceptions to the <code>ErrorBoundary</code>, and is released when the component is disposed: exactly what the attributes do.</li>
<li><code>Scope.Subscribe</code> and <code>IStateStore.Subscribe</code> are the lower-level APIs that services use (<a href="/events/tutorials/07-services-and-background-work">tutorial 07</a>). They do none of that for you.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="-best-practices">✅ Best practices</h2>

<ul>
<li><strong>Default to attributes.</strong> Use manual registration only for what attributes can't express, and say why in a comment.</li>
<li><strong>Call <code>base.RegisterSubscriptions(builder)</code> first</strong> in a manual override, so registrations from a base component aren't lost.</li>
<li><strong>Mixing? Use the <code>OnRegisterSubscriptions</code> hook</strong>, never a second override.</li>
<li><strong>Store handles in fields</strong> (<code>_price</code>) and read <code>.Value</code> in markup. Handles are released automatically.</li>
<li><strong>Pair every <code>Scope.Subscribe</code> with a dispose</strong> in <code>DisposeAsyncCore</code>, and wrap UI work in <code>InvokeAsync</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Use <code>@@key</code> when a parameter that a selector captured can change.</strong></li>
</ul>

<h2 id="common-mistakes">Common mistakes</h2>

<div class="table-container"><table class="table is-striped">
<thead>
<tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>InvalidOperationException: SubscriptionBuilder can only be used inside RegisterSubscriptions</code></td><td>Builder stored and used later</td><td>Use <code>Scope.Subscribe</code> for late subscriptions</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>RFEVT009</code></td><td>Override of <code>RegisterSubscriptions</code> in a component that also has attributes</td><td>Move the code into <code>partial void OnRegisterSubscriptions</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Tile shows the old symbol after its parameter changes</td><td>Selector captured the parameter at registration</td><td>Add <code>@@key</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Dispatcher</code> exceptions from a late subscription</td><td>Handler touches UI without <code>InvokeAsync</code></td><td>Wrap the body in <code>InvokeAsync</code></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>

